/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  cracking01_ethane_sundaram_froment -- STEAM CRACKING OF ETHANE with the
  molecular scheme of Sundaram & Froment (1977), against the pilot-plant
  product slate of Froment, Van de Steene & Van Damme (1976).

  THE SCHEME (Sundaram & Froment, Chem. Eng. Sci. 32:601, Model III of ethane
  cracking: Table 1 for the reactions and rate equations, Table 3 for A and E,
  the K_C values printed under Table 1; the same five reactions are Table XII
  of Froment et al.):
      (1) C2H6 <=> C2H4 + H2      (2) 2 C2H6 -> C3H8 + CH4   (first order)
      (5) C3H6 <=> C2H2 + CH4     (6) C2H2 + C2H4 -> C4H6
      (8) C2H4 + C2H6 -> C3H6 + CH4
  The reversible steps are written as a forward and a reverse law, k_f/K_C,
  with K_C of a van't Hoff fit to the three printed values (775, 800, 825 C).

  THE REACTOR.  The authors reduced their pilot data to isothermality at a
  reference temperature (the equivalent-reactor-volume concept), so this is one
  isothermal reactor at T_R = 840 C and 1.55 atm, ethane with 0.4 kg steam/kg
  (Table VIII, pilot column).  The pfr re-prices its volumetric flow along the bed
  (the vapour's Q = F_t v(T, P, z), C461), so the 40 % more moles the cracking
  makes are in the concentrations: ONE pfr, no segmentation.  The total
  volume, 15.004 L, is the one number the papers do not print for this run: it
  is chosen so the conversion is the published 59.1 %, and the case is judged on
  the product slate AT THAT CONVERSION, which is how the paper plots it.

  WHAT IT REPRODUCES, AND WHAT IT DOES NOT.  Published against engine, wt % of
  the ethane fed: C2H4 48.7 / 49.7 (+2 %, band 3 %), H2 3.71 / 3.77 (+1.6 %,
  band 6 %) -- inside the band declared before the run.  CH4 2.99 / 2.12,
  C3H6 1.05 / 0.43, C4H6 0.99 / 1.91 are OUTSIDE the declared bands (15, 35, 35 %):
  the scheme as printed, integrated exactly, does not give the table's
  methane, propylene and butadiene, and bin/curate/check_cracking_yields.py
  pins those three distances by name.  The table's ethane (39.0) and its own
  conversion (59.1 -> 40.9) disagree and are not compared.  See README.md.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

units
(
    {
        name        coil;
        type        pfr;
        in          feed;
        outputs     ( product );
        operation   { V_R 0.015004; nSteps 2000; }
        reactions   ( eth_dehydro eth_hydro eth_to_c3h8 c3h6_to_c2h2 c2h2_to_c3h6 c2h2_c2h4_to_c4h6 c2h4_c2h6_to_c3h6 );
    }
);
